  "observations": "<h3>Observed failure: Church.</h3><p>The reproduced raw-pixel baseline leaves an obvious red/cyan split around the church. Its red displacement is (64, 267) in (dy, dx) order. Broad low-texture sky and water, cross-channel brightness differences, and a coarse-level mismatch are plausible contributors; once a wrong coarse estimate is chosen, the ±3 refinements may not recover. The historical saved Church experiment is shown separately, with its original settings unverified.</p><h3>Local ghosts and surviving artifacts.</h3><p>Harvesters retains color fringes around some people. Movement between exposures is a plausible explanation, not a confirmed diagnosis from the composite alone. Self portrait retains a vivid green patch near the lower-right corner even after automatic cropping. This patch occupies only part of a row or column, so the detector's majority test does not necessarily remove it.</p>"
